# Deployment

Do not create the Cloudflare project, do not add the workflow, do not set secrets, and do not upload a build until the user explicitly approves a deploy.

When they approve, follow `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` from the top and stop at the first failed check. Report the check and the URL. Do not continue past a failure.

The Pages project `detro` already exists and is Direct Upload. Do not create a second project and do not connect it to Git.

- Production is Cloudflare Pages only. Project name `detro`. Public URL `https://detro.pages.dev`.
- GitHub Actions runs `npm ci`, `npm test`, and `npm run build`, then Wrangler uploads `dist`. Pages does not also build from Git.
- A pull request from this repository uploads a preview. A push to `main` uploads production. `npm run smoke` is not part of the job.
- Fail the job if `dist` has more than 20,000 files or any file over 25 MiB.
- Do not deploy `data/en/routes/`, `data/en/fares/`, `data/en/first-last/`, `data/hi/`, `scripts/`, `detro.archives/`, `curls/`, or `prompt.md`.
- No Vercel project, Pages Functions, Workers, R2, KV, D1, analytics, or a paid add-on.
- `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` are GitHub Actions secrets. Never commit them or print them.
